[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hey folks! Completely new to Veil. Are there any use cases for verifying or synthesizing  traces in lean according to a some kind of specification, like a temporal logic formula or an assume-guarantee contract? This problem has become increasingly important in robotics and control theory.</p>",
        "id": 583265593,
        "sender_full_name": "Hans Riess",
        "timestamp": 1775136156
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi! Currently we don't have concrete use cases or built-in support for that kind of trace-level verification or synthesis in Veil. </p>\n<p>A somewhat related direction we are exploring is the verification of liveness properties, which also involves temporal formulas. I shared some more details in this thread: <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"537982\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/537982-Veil/topic/Liveness.20proofs/with/581352661\">#Veil &gt; Liveness proofs</a> </p>\n<p>I'd also be curious if you have a concrete use case in mind, or any related work in robotics or control that we could take a look at.</p>",
        "id": 583270266,
        "sender_full_name": "Qiyuan Zhao",
        "timestamp": 1775137351
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"689027\">Qiyuan Zhao</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/537982-Veil/topic/robotics.20.26.20control/near/583270266\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>concrete use case</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>one concrete example is motion planning where you assume the continuous state space (usually a region of physical space) admits a partition into regions so that atomic propositions are of the form <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi^i_r</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0717em;vertical-align:-0.247em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8247em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.453em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">r</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.247em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> = \"Agent <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">i</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6595em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">i</span></span></span></span> has state partition <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">r</span></span></span></span>. then, a \"mission\" is specified by a temporal logic formula. the \"verification\" problem is to check whether all possible trajectories of the system satisfy the formula <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">φ</span></span></span></span>; the \"synthesis\" problem is to find at least one trajectory that satisfies the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varphi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">φ</span></span></span></span> which is equivalent to the verification problem for <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">¬</mi><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\neg \\varphi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">¬</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">φ</span></span></span></span>.</p>",
        "id": 583490784,
        "sender_full_name": "Hans Riess",
        "timestamp": 1775234737
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>another example that builds on top of this (which at least has the vibe of dependent type theory) is assume-guarantee contract theory where a \"contract\" consists of a set of assumptions (e.g., <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">⟦</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mtext>assume</mtext></msub><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">⟧</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\llbracket \\varphi_{\\text{assume}} \\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\"><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.1778em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">φ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">assume</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.1778em;\"></span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span></span></span></span></span> ) and a set of guarantees (e.g., <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">⟦</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mtext>guarantee</mtext></msub><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">⟧</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\llbracket \\varphi_{\\text{guarantee}} \\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\"><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.1778em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">φ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">guarantee</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.1778em;\"></span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span></span></span></span></span>) and you need to verify that a behavior (like a trajectory of a robot) that satisfies the assumptions (e.g. location of obstacles), provides the guarantees (e.g. reaching a target location quickly enough)</p>",
        "id": 583491339,
        "sender_full_name": "Hans Riess",
        "timestamp": 1775235006
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for the detailed explanation. This is really helpful!</p>\n<p>These examples are very interesting. I'll need to take some time to look into the relevant papers more carefully later.</p>",
        "id": 583691077,
        "sender_full_name": "Qiyuan Zhao",
        "timestamp": 1775399000
    }
]